            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Berkshire Hathaway's future without Buffett: The bull & bear case",
            "description": "<p>Berkshire Hathaway (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-B\">BRK-B</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-A\">BRK-A</a>) Chairman and CEO Warren Buffett is set to pass over the chief executive reins to his successor and current vice chair Greg Abel on January 1, 2026. Buffett will remain on the company's board as chairman.</p>\n<p>Most investors can only remember Berkshire's long-standing performance with Buffett at the helm. So how is Wall Street viewing the stock now that the \"Oracle of Omaha\" is on his way out?</p>\n<p>FBB Capital Partners Senior Portfolio Manager Mel Casey presents the bull and bear cases for Berkshire shares in 2026 to <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a>.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/asking-for-a-trend/\">Asking for a Trend</a>.</p>",
